<blockquote class="uncited"><div>hi. download link?</div></blockquote>TL;DR: Files are not offered for download by TYT. Please contact them via <a href="mailto:overseas@tyt888.com">overseas@tyt888.com</a> as per earlier posts. You may of course also approach me by email (check details via QRZ.com) and receive a copy of what TYT had provided to me in late July...<br><br>Long version with some additional background details:<br><br>As per my earlier post I had contacted TYT via email and received a wetransfer link for the “V5” files (which has expired in the meanwhile). In parallel, I was in touch with the team at Passion Radio to clarify on the correct files as their website had somehow opposing FW statements for V4 and V5 at that time. We were a larger team of OMs that all ordered V5 devices from their “final stock” and so I wanted to get clarification on according TYT firmware for these – just in case. (Note: V5 devices are no longer available from them as of today. Assume TYT went back to include STM CPUs based on improved availability…)<br><br>Passion Radio later on forwarded an email from TYT services to me stating the following:<br><br>“Actually the name you called V5 its same as V4, even the CPS software and firmware. Both are compatible . just one have silk STM32 another one didn’t have silk. please noted that . […]”<br><br>That was when Passion Radio also updated the product details on the website, so they now provide V4 firmware for V4 &amp; V5 devices:<br><br><a href="https://www.passion-radio.com/mobile/md9600-2252.html" class="postlink">https://www.passion-radio.com/mobile/md9600-2252.html</a> (V5, nonSTM32)<br><a href="https://www.passion-radio.com/mobile/md9600-505.html" class="postlink">https://www.passion-radio.com/mobile/md9600-505.html</a> (V4, STM32)<br><br>Yet, TYT provided me with a dedicated V5 FW just a few weeks before and the files I had received clearly differ from what is now available for download at Passion Radio on the V5 page. My assumption is that the “V4 files” were updated later on to also cover nonSTM32 devices.<br><br>Again, I neither tried TYT’s “V4” nor “V5” files to bring back any of the MD-9600 to original FW so far. Simply because my devices are all running so smoothly with OpenMD9600  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_razz.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":P" title="Razz"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2090">DG1GMY</a> — Sat Oct 21, 2023 12:44 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
