Try getting in touch with TYT customer service. They have in the past been good at supplying firmware. <br><br>The 026 at the beginning of the firmware version indicates it is for the V5 radio.  TYT normally release three versions of each firmware.  <br><br>006.xxx  = V1 V2 and V3 radios<br>016.xxx = V4 radios<br>026.xxx = V5 radios.<br><br><br>The radio version numbers are what we use for OpenGD77, they may not be the same as those used by TYT. <br><br><br>Colin G4EML.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Wed Jul 26, 2023 6:58 pm</p><hr />
